# Seed Data Generation Engine Implementation Plan

The goal is to create an automated seed script (`prisma/seed.ts`) capable of rapidly populating the SQLite database with 10,000 realistic employee records and their associated salary histories, maintaining strong referential integrity.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Because SQLite has parameterized query limits, inserting 10,000 records row-by-row via standard `prisma.employee.create()` would be incredibly slow.
> I plan to bypass this by pre-generating standard `UUIDv4` identifiers for all entities directly in Node.js, compiling them into large arrays, and inserting them using **chunked `createMany()` blocks** (e.g., chunks of 500-1000). This should reduce the seed time from minutes to just a few seconds.

## Open Questions

1. **Dummy Data Library**: Standard projects use libraries like `faker.js` to generate names and emails. Is it acceptable to install `@faker-js/faker` as a `devDependency` to generate the 10,000 unique realistic names, or would you prefer I build a small static array of names to randomly combine (to keep dependencies strictly zero)? I recommend `@faker-js/faker` for realistic variety.
2. **Seed Reset**: Should the seed script automatically wipe the existing database tables before inserting the new 10,000 records to ensure a clean slate on every run? (I will plan to wipe the database by default).

## Proposed Changes

